<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    CMP-CNT-001 (content compiler/validator) and CMP-CNT-002 (runtime content
    registry). Owns strict source models, schemas, the compiler, immutable
    runtime definitions, and behavior-registration contracts.

    Accepted project boundary (docs/technical/115 § Accepted project boundary):
      allowed project dependencies: .NET base libraries only
      Godot types allowed:          No

    Intentionally has no ProjectReference and no PackageReference. First types
    land in TASK-DAT-001-001.
  -->

  <ItemGroup Label="Test-only access to internals (doc 91 § Test project separation)">
    <!--
      Exactly one grant, to this project's own mirror test project. Every type here is
      internal, so without it no behaviour of this project is testable at all. doc 91:
      "Test-only access occurs through explicit diagnostic APIs/assemblies, not reflection
      into private state", and the assembly route is the sanctioned one.

      It is for behaviour that genuinely cannot be observed through the public contract. A
      repeated need for it is a missing diagnostic API - QUA-003 needs one anyway for the
      debug overlay and command palette - not a reason to widen test coupling to
      implementation detail. No other project appears here: MechaMiner.Game.Tests
      deliberately consumes the public contract, which is the point of that project.
    -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="MechaMiner.Content.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
